              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Incorrect. Remember that a solution with dissolved solutes will begin precipitation of the solute when the solution contains the maximum amount of dissolved solute, in other words, when the solution is saturated with the solute. Within a saturated solution, an equilibrium exists between dissolved and undissolved solute, and the equilibrium constant for solubility equilibria is called the solubility product constant, "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "K"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "sp"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ". In other words, a precipitate will form when the actual concentrations are equal to or greater than "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "K"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "sp"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ". Write the correct chemical equation for the solubility equilibrium and correct equilibrium expression, then calculate the reaction quotient "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "Q"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " and compare its value to equilibrium constant "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "K"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "sp"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ". If "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "Q"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " is less than "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "K"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", then more products need to form, meaning more solid can dissolve before equilibrium is reached. If "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "Q"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " is greater than "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "K"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", then more reactants need to form, meaning the dissolved solutes need to precipitate to reach equilibrium. If "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "Q"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " is equal to "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "K"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", then the reaction is at equilibrium, and precipitate will begin to form."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "0fsaatz7xp5858b",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
